<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Sonic Collective" description="How Sonic Collective handles browser preferences and YouTube playback." canonicalPath="/privacy/" currentPath="/privacy/">
  <section class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Your visit</p><h1>Privacy</h1></section>
  <section class="page-copy wrap">
    <p>Sonic Collective uses your browser’s reduced-motion preference to limit decorative movement. If you pause motion, that choice is stored in this browser so it can be remembered on your next visit.</p>
    <h2>Site analytics</h2><p>We use Vercel Web Analytics to understand page visits and traffic. It uses cookie-free analytics. Search query text is removed from the page URLs we send. When custom events are enabled, we measure Watch, artist-profile, and collaboration clicks using fixed event names and catalog IDs.</p>
    <h2>YouTube playback</h2><p>Full performances play through YouTube. The YouTube player is loaded only after you choose to play a performance, and YouTube may receive information about your visit when it loads. Following an external YouTube link is subject to YouTube’s own privacy practices.</p>
    <p>This page describes the site’s current behavior; it does not promise that third-party services collect no data.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
